The bug was a classic off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to get the second element instead of `parts[0]` to get the first element. This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError since there's no index 1

The fix changed the index from `[1]` to `[0]`, and now both tests pass successfully.
